     - **Solution:** You could introduce a small sleep (e.g., `time.sleep(0.1)`) after calling `start()` to allow some time to have elapsed before checking the elapsed time. However, this approach could introduce timing issues in unit tests, making it less reliable. A better design could involve checking time on-demand considering there's an assumption of time passing. 

