n is responsible for initializing a new puzzle with the selected image and difficulty. It demonstrates the loading of a specific image into the puzzle.\n\n---\n|Case|:**save_progress**\n```pseudocode\nCLASS Game:\n    FUNCTION save_progress():\n        OPEN 'progress.txt' FOR WRITING AS f:\n            WRITE self.current_puzzle.image + '|' + self.timer.get_elapsed_time()  // Save image and elapsed time\n\nFUNCTION get_elapsed_time():\n    IF self.start_time IS None:\n        RETURN '00:00'\n    ELAPSED TIME CALCULATION  // Calculate the time since start\n```\n- **Key Functionality**: This functionality allows players to save their progress in a text file, maintaining the current image and the elapsed time since starting the puzzle.\n\n---\n", "|Case|:**load_progress**\n```pseudocode\nFUNCTION load_progress(user: STRING) RETURNS STRING\n    OPEN 'progress.txt' FOR READ AS file\n        FOR EACH line IN file\n            IF line STARTS WITH user\n                RETURN SPLIT line by '|' AT index 1  // Extract progress data\n            ENDIF\n        ENDFOR\n    RETURN None  // No matching user found\nEND FUNCTION\n```\n- **Key Functionality**: The load_progress function retrieves saved user progress from the progress file, allowing a user to resume their game from a specified state.\n\n---\n|Case|:**start_timer**\n```pseudocode\nCLASS Timer:\n    FUNCTION start():\n        SET self.start_time = TIME NOW  // Start the timer at the current time\n\nFUNCTION get_elapsed_time():\n    IF self.start_time IS None:\n        RETURN '00:00'  // Return default if timer not started\n```\n- **Key Functionality**: This segment manages the timer for the game, where `start()` records the current time. The `get_elapsed_time()` method calculates how long the timer has been running.\n\n---"]
